### Reproducible example

The bug report and example were adapted from: https://github.com/pola-rs/pyo3-polars/issues/51
I re-report this issue because the pyo3-polars repo is archived, but I couldn't find this issue here.

```rust
use pyo3::prelude::*;
use pyo3::types::PyModule;
use pyo3_polars::PyDataFrame;
use std::ffi::CString;

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    Python::initialize();

    let code = CString::new(
        r#"
import polars as pl

def get_sorted_df():
    df = pl.DataFrame(
        {
            "a": [9, 2, 0],
            "b": [6.0, 5.0, 4.0],
            "c": ["a", "c", "b"],
        }
    )
    return df.sort("a")

def get_is_sorted():
    df = get_sorted_df()
    return str(df["a"].is_sorted())
"#,
    )?;

    let file_name = CString::new("embedded_polars.py")?;
    let module_name = CString::new("embedded_polars")?;

    Python::attach(|py| -> PyResult<()> {
        let py_module = PyModule::from_code(
            py,
            code.as_c_str(),
            file_name.as_c_str(),
            module_name.as_c_str(),
        )?;

        let get_sorted_df = py_module.getattr("get_sorted_df")?;
        let df = get_sorted_df.call0()?.extract::<PyDataFrame>()?.0;

        println!("df: {:?}", df);

        let is_sorted_flag = df.column("a").unwrap().is_sorted_flag();
        println!("Rust is_sorted_flag(): {:?}", is_sorted_flag);

        let get_is_sorted = py_module.getattr("get_is_sorted")?;
        let py_is_sorted = get_is_sorted.call0()?.extract::<String>()?;

        println!("Python is_sorted(): {:?}", py_is_sorted);

        Ok(())
    })?;
```

### Log output

```shell
Rust is_sorted_flag(): Not
Python is_sorted(): "True"
```

### Issue description

When converting DataFrames from and to python the flags are lost. This also happens for registered plugin functions

### Expected behavior

If a flag is set in python, then when converting to rust using PyDataFrame the flags are preserved.

### Installed versions

<details>
pyo3 = { version = "0.28" }
pyo3-polars = { version = "0.27", features = ["derive"] }
</details>
